---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Electromagnetism Cheat Sheet | Free Maxwell's Equations & Applications"
  description="Complete electromagnetism cheat sheet with Maxwell's equations and applications. Free download for physics and engineering students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Electromagnetism<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Maxwell's equations and applications. From electrostatics to electromagnetic waves.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Maxwell's Equations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gauss's Law (Electric)</h3>
        <pre><code>∮ E · dA = Q/ε₀

Electric flux through closed surface equals charge enclosed divided by permittivity.</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gauss's Law (Magnetic)</h3>
        <pre><code>∮ B · dA = 0

No magnetic monopoles exist.</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Faraday's Law</h3>
        <pre><code>∮ E · dl = -dΦ_B/dt

Changing magnetic field induces electric field.</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Ampere-Maxwell Law</h3>
        <pre><code>∮ B · dl = μ₀I + μ₀ε₀ dΦ_E/dt

Magnetic field from current and changing electric field.</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Electric Fields</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Coulomb's Law</h3>
        <pre><code>F = kQq/r²
k = 1/(4πε₀) = 8.99 × 10⁹</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Electric Field</h3>
        <pre><code>E = F/q = kQ/r²
V = Ed (uniform field)
C = Q/V = ε₀A/d</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Magnetic Fields</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Force on Current</h3>
        <pre><code>F = BIL sin θ
F = Bqv sin θ</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Electromagnetic Induction</h3>
        <pre><code>EMF = -N dΦ/dt (Faraday)
Φ = BA cos θ (flux)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
